cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OEBC or its catalog, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "OEBC: Open Exposure Baseline Catalog"
abstract: >-
  OEBC is a daily, machine-readable CVE exposure baseline. It fetches every
  CVE from the NVD CVE API, joins each one by CVE ID with its FIRST EPSS
  score and percentile and its CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities entry,
  and adds two derived fields: an exposure tier (CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM or
  LOW) and an actionable flag. The catalog is published as gzip-compressed
  JSON at openastra.org, with a versioned JSON Schema, and is built by a
  Python package and command-line tool, oebc.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sadayamuthu
    given-names: Karthikeyan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3539-6048"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: MIT
